-- title:
--   Eigenspace rank four when p ∣ L and ρ̄ is non-ordinary
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a complete discrete valuation ring of characteristic zero with finite residue field $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}(\mathcal O)$, let $p\neq 2$ be a prime with $p\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$, and let $\bar\rho$ be a two-dimensional representation of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ over $k$ factoring through a finite level and absolutely irreducible (irreducible after base change to $\overline{k}$). Let $S,S_{\min}$ be finite sets of primes with $p\in S_{\min}\subseteq S$, such that a prime $q\neq p$ lies in $S_{\min}$ exactly when $\bar\rho$ is ramified at $q$, and such that for $q\in S_{\min}$, $q\neq p$, every inertia element at $q$ has characteristic polynomial $(X-1)^2$ in $\bar\rho$. Let $N,L\geq 1$ satisfy: every prime divisor of $N$ lies in $S$; $p^2\nmid N$; every $q\in S_{\min}\setminus\{p\}$ divides $N$; every prime $q\neq p$ dividing $N$ but not in $S_{\min}$ has $q^2\mid N$; no prime $q\neq p$ has $q^3\mid N$; $L\mid N$, $N$ and $L$ have the same prime divisors, $q^2\mid N$ implies $q^2\mid L$, and no prime cube divides $L$. Assume the integral lattice in weight-two cusp forms for $\Gamma_0(N)$ spans the whole space over $\mathbb C$ ([`CuspForm.HasIntegralStructure N 2`](def/CuspForm_IntegralStructure.html#L6)). Let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from the anemic Hecke algebra $\mathbb T=$ [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) (the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}$ of weight-two cusp forms generated by the Hecke generators away from $S$) to $k$ with $\mathrm{charpoly}(\bar\rho(\sigma))=X^2-\theta(T_\ell)X+\ell$ for every prime $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\notin S$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in which $\ell$ is a nonunit, and every $\sigma$ that is a Frobenius at $\ell$ for $P$. Let $M$ be a module over the localisation $\mathbb T_\theta=$ [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S 𝒪 θ`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) and over $\mathcal O$, compatibly, and $B$ an $\mathcal O$-bilinear form on $M$, and assume [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.IsCornerRealization`](def/CuspForm_HeckeModuleCornerRealization.html#L19): there are a commuting family of operators indexed by the generators `Gen L S`, a residual eigensystem $\bar\theta$ on those generators, an idempotent splitting $Sp$ of the algebra they generate, an index $i_0$ and an $\mathcal O$-algebra map from the corner ring $Sp.\mathrm{CornerRing}\,i_0$ to $k$ inducing $\bar\theta$, such that the corner submodule cut out by $Sp.e\,i_0$ inside $H^1(\Gamma_H(L),\mathcal O)$ consists of parabolic classes and is $\mathcal O$-linearly isomorphic to $M$ by a map intertwining the action of $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell\notin S$, $\ell\nmid N$) with `heckeT` and pulling back the period pairing [`CuspForm.Bfam₀`](def/CuspForm_CornerPairingFamily.html#L140) to $B$, while $\bar\theta(T_\ell)=\theta(T_\ell)$ for $\ell\notin S$, $\ell\nmid L$, $\ell\nmid N$, $\bar\theta(U_q)=0$ whenever $q^2\mid L$, and $\bar\theta(U_p)\neq 0$ whenever $p\mid L$ and $\bar\rho$ is ordinary at $p$. Let $\mathcal O'$ be a further complete discrete valuation ring of characteristic zero with finite residue field, module-finite over $\mathcal O$ via a local algebra map, and $\chi:\mathbb T_\theta\to\mathcal O'$ an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism. Assume finally that $p\mid L$ and that $\bar\rho$, viewed as an adic representation, is not ordinary at $p$ (there is a valuation subring over $p$ admitting no $\mathcal O$-line spanned by a basis vector that is stable under the decomposition group and on whose quotient inertia acts trivially). Then the intersection, over all $t\in\mathbb T_\theta$, of the $\chi(t)$-eigenspaces of the $\mathcal O'$-base change of multiplication by $t$ on $M$ has $\mathcal O'$-rank exactly $4$.
--
--   This is the non-ordinary case of the local multiplicity computation for a corner realisation of the parabolic cohomology of $\Gamma_H(L)$ at cube-free level: when $p$ divides $L$ and $\bar\rho$ is not ordinary at $p$, each character $\chi$ of the localised anemic Hecke algebra occurs in the base-changed corner module with geometric multiplicity four. It feeds the comparison of ranks in [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.finrank_torsionBySet_ker_eq_four_mul_finrank_quotient_of_isCornerRealization_of_not_isOrdinaryAt_of_not_cube_dvd`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.finrank_torsionBySet_ker_eq_four_mul_finrank_quotient_of_isCornerRealization_of_not_isOrdinaryAt_of_not_cube_dvd), and rests on the newform-multiplicity count [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.newformMultiplicity_finrank_iInf_eigenspace_algebraicClosure_eq_of_isCornerRealization_of_not_cube_dvd`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.newformMultiplicity_finrank_iInf_eigenspace_algebraicClosure_eq_of_isCornerRealization_of_not_cube_dvd) together with the finiteness of $H^1(\Gamma_H(L),\mathcal O)$ over $\mathcal O$.
